1. AA-Briefcase-Lite (eval 4)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Eval 4 uses AA-Briefcase-Lite by Artificial Analysis, licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0.

  Source:   https://huggingface.co/datasets/ArtificialAnalysis/AA-Briefcase-Lite
  Revision: 4dec557b47d43867a1648c0974db1d8208c8b677

The dataset is NOT redistributed in this repository. `dbwm fetch eval4`
downloads the 166 files eval 4 needs from the publisher at the pinned revision
and verifies each against the sha256 manifest in dbwm/eval4/aa_manifest.json.
The downloaded copy lives in data/eval4/aa-briefcase-lite/ and
private/eval4/aa-briefcase-lite/, which are excluded from version control. Its
source pool contains documents from third parties; their rights are not
affected by this repository's licences.

Derived material shipped here, modified from the dataset under Apache-2.0 (a
copy of that licence is in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt):
  * dbwm/eval4/checker.py implements a heuristic, deterministic approximation
    of the twelve binary w1_t2 rubric checks, with numeric ranges anchored on
    the dataset's source files; its prose mode generates the CHECKLIST.md the
    checklist arms receive (a paraphrase of the rubric, not the rubric text).
  * dbwm/eval4/aa_manifest.json lists file paths and hashes at the pinned
    revision.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Optional dependency under the EUPL: formulas and schedula
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The optional extra `recalc` installs `formulas` (1.3.4) and `schedula`
(1.6.15), which are licensed under the European Union Public Licence
(EUPL-1.1 or later). They recalculate formulas in agent-written spreadsheets
for eval 4. They are not vendored and not installed by default; the code
imports them only if present.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Origin of the synthetic worlds
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The eval-1 companies and the business-unit model behind the eval-2 and eval-3
worlds were first authored as operating models in Differential AI Lab's
internal business-modelling product. This package ships them as standalone
JSON evaluated by its own Python engine (dbwm/eval1, dbwm/eval2); it has no
connection to that product, its registry or its live service.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Container image
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

docker/Dockerfile builds a local image from python:3.12-slim, Node.js,
@anthropic-ai/claude-code (pinned 2.1.287) and pinned Python packages. The
image is built by the user and not distributed with this repository; each
component remains under its own licence or terms of use, including
Anthropic's terms for Claude Code.
